# Direct Python dependencies for the live Sign2Text runtime â€” NVIDIA/CUDA profile.
# For machines WITHOUT an NVIDIA GPU, use requirements.runtime-cpu.in instead.
#
# Verified against the checked-in .venv on Python 3.11.9.
#
# Runtime app paths covered here:
# - backend/api_server.py
# - backend/new_Inference.py
# - backend/stt_backend.py
# - backend/tts_backend.py
# - backend/translate.py
# - start.py
#
# Intentionally excluded from the live-app runtime set:
# - offline keypoint-extraction and model-training tooling: maintained
#   privately, not published in this repository. Needs additional packages
#   such as pandas and tensorboard.
# - tests/: pytest-only dependencies. Use requirements.test.txt for validation.
#
# Environment/system requirements still outside pip:
# - external ASL checkpoint file
# - local webcam access
# - Ollama service + model
# - Google/Azure credentials
# - CUDA-compatible drivers/runtime for the GPU torch/onnxruntime builds below
#
# rtmlib 0.0.15 declares a dependency on the CPU-named "onnxruntime" package
# even when this project intentionally runs on the GPU build. The local
# compatibility metapackage below keeps the environment reproducible and makes
# pip's dependency checks consistent without changing the actual runtime engine.
#
# PyTorch CUDA wheels are distributed from the official PyTorch wheel index.
# Keeping the extra index explicit here makes fresh-machine installs reproducible
# without relying on per-user pip configuration.

./packaging/onnxruntime-meta/dist/onnxruntime-1.24.2-py3-none-any.whl
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu128

